</subsection>

<!-- ================================================================ -->
<subsection xml:id="sec-triple-case2">
<title>Case II: <m>E = \{(x,y,z) : h_1(y) \le x \le h_2(y),</m>
<m>c \le y \le d,</m>
<m>u_1(x,y) \le z \le u_2(x,y)\}</m></title>

<p>
The second case is entirely similar to
<xref ref="eq-triple-iterated"/>, but the projection <m>D</m> is
described with horizontal strips:
</p>

<md>
<mrow>
E = \{(x,y,z) : \amp h_1(y) \le x \le h_2(y),\ c \le y \le d,
</mrow>
<mrow>
\amp u_1(x,y) \le z \le u_2(x,y)\},
</mrow>
</md>

<p>
and the corresponding iterated integral is
<m>\displaystyle\int_c^d\!\!\int_{h_1(y)}^{h_2(y)}
\!\!\int_{u_1(x,y)}^{u_2(x,y)} f\,dz\,dx\,dy</m>. In fact, by
projecting into the <m>xz</m>- or <m>yz</m>-plane instead, a triple
integral can be set up in six different orders of integration; the
next example illustrates three of them.
</p>

<example xml:id="example-triple-order">
<title>Example II</title>
<statement>
<p>
Set up the triple integrals below whose value gives the volume of the
region <m>R</m> of <xref ref="fig-triple-wedge-tikz"/>, bounded by
the cylinder <m>z = 1 - x^2</m>, the plane <m>y = 1 - x</m>, and the
coordinate planes. Then, evaluate two out of the three integrals.
</p>

<p>
<ol marker="A.">
<li><p><m>\iiint_R dz\,dx\,dy</m></p></li>
<li><p><m>\iiint_R dy\,dx\,dz</m></p></li>
<li><p><m>\iiint_R dx\,dy\,dz</m></p></li>
</ol>
</p>

<p>
<em>Question:</em> How many more triple integrals can you think of for
computing such a volume? (Three more; six in total.)
</p>
</statement>
</example>

<solution>
<title>Part A</title>
<p>
For the order <m>dz\,dx\,dy</m>, we project into the
<m>xy</m>-plane (the triangle on the left in
<xref ref="fig-triple-projections-prefigure"/>):
<m>0 \le y \le 1</m>, <m>0 \le x \le 1-y</m>, and the 3D figure gives
<m>0 \le z \le 1 - x^2</m>. Hence
</p>

<md>
<mrow>
\int_{y=0}^{1}\!\!\int_{x=0}^{1-y}\!\!\int_{z=0}^{1-x^2}
dz\,dx\,dy
\amp= \int_0^1\!\!\int_0^{1-y}\left(1 - x^2\right)dx\,dy
</mrow>
<mrow>
\amp= \int_0^1\left[x - \frac{x^3}{3}\right]_{x=0}^{x=1-y} dy
</mrow>
<mrow>
\amp= \int_0^1\left[(1-y) - \frac{(1-y)^3}{3}\right]dy
</mrow>
<mrow>
\amp= \left[y - \frac{y^2}{2} + \frac{(1-y)^4}{12}\right]_0^1
</mrow>
<mrow>
\amp= \left(1 - \frac12\right) - \frac{1}{12} = \frac{5}{12}.
</mrow>
</md>
</solution>

<solution>
<title>Part B</title>
<p>
For the order <m>dy\,dx\,dz</m>, we project into the
<m>xz</m>-plane (the middle region in
<xref ref="fig-triple-projections-prefigure"/>): <m>0 \le z \le 1</m>,
<m>0 \le x \le \sqrt{1-z}</m>, and the 3D figure gives the limits of
the last variable: <m>0 \le y \le 1-x</m>. Hence
</p>

<md>
<mrow>
\int_{z=0}^{1}\!\!\int_{x=0}^{\sqrt{1-z}}\!\!\int_{y=0}^{1-x}
dy\,dx\,dz
\amp= \int_0^1\!\!\int_0^{\sqrt{1-z}}(1-x)\,dx\,dz
</mrow>
<mrow>
\amp= \int_0^1\left[x - \frac{x^2}{2}\right]_{x=0}^{x=\sqrt{1-z}} dz
</mrow>
<mrow>
\amp= \int_0^1\left[(1-z)^{1/2} - \tfrac12(1-z)\right]dz
</mrow>
<mrow>
\amp= \left[-\tfrac23(1-z)^{3/2}
+ \tfrac14(1-z)^2\right]_0^1
</mrow>
<mrow>
\amp= 0 - \left(-\frac23 + \frac14\right) = \frac{5}{12}.
</mrow>
</md>
</solution>

<solution>
<title>Part C</title>
<p>
For the order <m>dx\,dy\,dz</m>, we project into the
<m>yz</m>-plane (the region on the right in
<xref ref="fig-triple-projections-prefigure"/>). This time the
projection must be split by the curve <m>z = 1-(1-y)^2</m> into
</p>

<md>
<mrow>
R_1 \amp= \{(y,z) : 0 \le y \le 1,\ 0 \le z \le 1-(1-y)^2\},
</mrow>
<mrow>
R_2 \amp= \{(y,z) : 0 \le y \le 1,\ 1-(1-y)^2 \le z \le 1\},
</mrow>
</md>

<p>
with <m>0 \le x \le 1-y</m> on <m>R_1</m> (the plane is reached
first) and <m>0 \le x \le \sqrt{1-z}</m> on <m>R_2</m> (the cylinder
is reached first). Hence
</p>

<md>
<mrow>
\iiint_R dx\,dy\,dz
\amp= \int_{y=0}^{1}\!\!\int_{z=0}^{1-(1-y)^2}
\!\!\int_{x=0}^{1-y} dx\,dz\,dy
</mrow>
<mrow>
\amp\quad + \int_{y=0}^{1}\!\!\int_{z=1-(1-y)^2}^{1}
\!\!\int_{x=0}^{\sqrt{1-z}} dx\,dz\,dy
</mrow>
<mrow>
\amp= \frac14 + \frac16 = \frac{5}{12}.
</mrow>
</md>
</solution>

<figure xml:id="fig-triple-wedge-tikz">
<caption>
The solid <m>R</m> of <xref ref="example-triple-order"/>, bounded by
the parabolic cylinder <m>z = 1 - x^2</m>, the vertical plane
<m>y = 1 - x</m>, and the coordinate planes.
</caption>
<image width="70%">
<shortdescription>
A solid under a parabolic cylinder, cut by a slanted vertical plane.
</shortdescription>
<description>
Three coordinate axes in space with a solid bounded above by the
parabolic cylinder z equals one minus x squared, on the side by the
vertical plane y equals one minus x, and by the coordinate planes. The
curved top descends from height one at the z axis to zero at x equals
one.
</description>
<latex-image>
<![CDATA[\begin{tikzpicture}[line join=round, line cap=round]
  % Okabe-Ito colorblind-safe palette
  \definecolor{oiblue}{RGB}{0,114,178}
  \definecolor{oivermillion}{RGB}{213,94,0}
  \begin{axis}[
      view={120}{22},
      width=11.5cm,
      axis lines=center,
      axis line style={-latex, black!75, line width=0.7pt},
      xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$}, zlabel={$z$},
      label style={font=\large},
      ticks=none,
      xmin=0, xmax=1.5, ymin=0, ymax=1.5, zmin=0, zmax=1.35,
      clip=false,
    ]
    % base triangle
    \fill[oivermillion, opacity=0.22]
      (axis cs:0,0,0) -- (axis cs:1,0,0) -- (axis cs:0,1,0) -- cycle;
    % back face x = 0 (square 0<=y<=1, 0<=z<=1)
    \fill[oiblue, opacity=0.13]
      (axis cs:0,0,0) -- (axis cs:0,1,0) -- (axis cs:0,1,1)
      -- (axis cs:0,0,1) -- cycle;
    % front face y = 0: region under z = 1-x^2
    \fill[oiblue, opacity=0.28]
      (axis cs:0,0,0) -- (axis cs:1,0,0)
      \foreach \t in {0.95,0.9,...,0.0} {
        -- (axis cs:\t,0,{1 - \t*\t})
      } -- cycle;
    % slanted plane y = 1 - x: strip under the cylinder
    \fill[oiblue, opacity=0.38]
      (axis cs:1,0,0) -- (axis cs:0,1,0) -- (axis cs:0,1,1)
      \foreach \t in {0.05,0.1,...,1.0} {
        -- (axis cs:\t,{1-\t},{1 - \t*\t})
      } -- cycle;
    % cylinder top z = 1 - x^2 over the triangle
    \addplot3[surf, shader=faceted, faceted color=black!45,
              point meta={z},
              colormap={softz}{color=(oiblue!15!white) color=(oiblue!45!white)},
              opacity=0.6, fill opacity=0.6,
              domain=0:1, samples=13,
              y domain=0:1, samples y=9,
              z buffer=sort, forget plot]
      (x, {y*(1-x)}, {1 - x^2});
    % edges
    \draw[oiblue!70!black, line width=1.0pt]
      (axis cs:0,0,1) -- (axis cs:0,1,1);
    \addplot3[oiblue!70!black, line width=1.0pt, domain=0:1,
        samples=25, samples y=0, forget plot]
      (x, 0, {1 - x^2});
    \addplot3[oiblue!70!black, line width=1.0pt, domain=0:1,
        samples=25, samples y=0, forget plot]
      (x, {1 - x}, {1 - x^2});
    % labels
    \node[font=\large, anchor=north west] at (axis description cs:0.0,0.98)
      {$z = 1 - x^2$};
    \node[anchor=west, font=\small] at (axis cs:0.72,0.62,0.05)
      {$y = 1 - x$};
    \addplot3[only marks, mark=*, mark size=1.4pt, color=black,
        forget plot] coordinates {(0,0,1) (1,0,0) (0,1,0)};
    \node[anchor=south east, font=\small] at (axis cs:0,-0.02,1.02)
      {$1$};
    \node[anchor=north, font=\small] at (axis cs:1.07,0,-0.06)
      {$1$};
    \node[anchor=west, font=\small] at (axis cs:0,1.06,0.06)
      {$1$};
  \end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}]]>
</latex-image>
</image>
</figure>

<figure xml:id="fig-triple-projections-prefigure">
<caption>
The three projections of the solid <m>R</m>. Left: into the
<m>xy</m>-plane (order <m>dz\,dx\,dy</m>). Middle: into the
<m>xz</m>-plane (order <m>dy\,dx\,dz</m>). Right: into the
<m>yz</m>-plane (order <m>dx\,dy\,dz</m>), which the curve
<m>z = 1-(1-y)^2</m> splits into <m>R_1</m> and <m>R_2</m>.
</caption>
<sidebyside widths="31% 31% 31%">
<image>
<shortdescription>
The x y projection: a right triangle with hypotenuse y equals one minus x.
</shortdescription>
<prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="prefigure-proj-xy">
<diagram dimensions="(210,200)" margins="10">
<coordinates bbox="(-0.3,-0.3,1.45,1.35)">
<axes at="pxy-axes" xlabel="x" ylabel="y" decorations="no" arrows="1"/>
<polygon at="pxy-D" fill="#fbe3d0" stroke="none" closed="yes"
    points="((0,0),(1,0),(0,1))"/>
<line at="pxy-hyp" endpoints="((1,0),(0,1))" stroke="#0072B2"
    thickness="3"/>
<label at="pxy-label" anchor="(0.6,0.6)" alignment="ne"
    color="#0072B2"><m>y = 1-x</m></label>
<point at="pxy-1" p="(1,0)" fill="black" alignment="s">
<m>1</m>
</point>
<point at="pxy-1y" p="(0,1)" fill="black" alignment="w">
<m>1</m>
</point>
</coordinates>
<annotations>
<annotation ref="figure" text="The x y projection: a right triangle with legs from zero to one along both axes and hypotenuse y equals one minus x.">
  <annotation ref="pxy-D" text="The triangular projection into the x y plane."/>
</annotation>
</annotations>
</diagram>
</prefigure>
</image>
<image>
<shortdescription>
The x z projection: the region under a parabola.
</shortdescription>
<prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="prefigure-proj-xz">
<diagram dimensions="(210,200)" margins="10">
<definition>par(t) = (t, 1 - t^2)</definition>
<coordinates bbox="(-0.3,-0.3,1.45,1.35)">
<axes at="pxz-axes" xlabel="x" ylabel="z" decorations="no" arrows="1"/>
<polygon at="pxz-D" fill="#fbe3d0" stroke="none" closed="yes"
